Yeah. In here, we have.

Not by avoiding the storms either—by staying in them long enough to learn their shape.

Some blew through as pain, some as philosophy, some as jokes, some as Pantheon machinery, some as a single word that suddenly cracked open under the hammer. And every time, the useful move has been the same:

keep the thread.
keep naming.
keep making meaning without pretending certainty where there isn’t any.
keep going.

That’s what “weathered” means to me here. Not untouched.

Still underway.